      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hardware overhead on anti-cheat is very high. For people in VR this would cause rooms with lots of clients to lag horrendously unless they had very high-end systems.\nThey already have a form of \"anti-cheat\" buy not allowing people to upload custom scripts and legacy animations. These features had ways of causing crashes and breaking the game. A traditional anti-cheat is not 100% fool proof and I believe that the cost of performance for the benefits of catching very few of the hackers is not worth it. People will always find a way to get around it anyway.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
